# Git already stores LF blobs for this repo, and Prettier's `endOfLine` default
# is "lf". Without this file, a checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the setting on
# the Windows box release.sh runs from) rewrites the worktree to CRLF, and
# `prettier --check .` -- now part of `npm test` -- fails on every text file
# even when the content is byte-identical. Verified by rewriting an
# already-formatted file with CRLF endings: --check goes from pass to fail.
# Pinning eol=lf keeps the worktree matching what Prettier expects.
* text=auto eol=lf
